# GH-256: `forjar dist` output. Release builds it into /tmp/dist-output; a copy
# committed at the repo root in March went stale against the maintained
# install.sh and carried 7 bashrs SEC findings the real one does not.
/dist-output/
.dogfood/
.pv/

# pmat writes a `.pmat/` cache wherever it is INVOKED, not just at the repo
# root. A run from src/verb/ or tests/ leaves a nested one holding tdg-*.db
# scratch; on 2026-08-23 a `git add -A src/` staged eight of them.
#
# Unanchored so it catches every depth, which also covers the root — that is
# deliberate.
#
# NOTHING UNDER `.pmat/` CAN BE TRACKED, and no `!` negation here can change
# that (#401). pmat writes its OWN `.pmat/.gitignore` containing `*`, with a
# header saying the directory is derived and rebuilt on demand; a .gitignore in
# a deeper directory outranks every pattern in a shallower one, so a negation at
# this level is unreachable. MEASURED, after a `pmat tdg baseline update` run
# dropped that file in: `git check-ignore --no-index -v .pmat/cb200-baseline.json`
# -> `.pmat/.gitignore:10:*`, with `!/.pmat/cb200-baseline.json` sitting right
# here and doing nothing. It is untracked too, so it appears only on machines
# where pmat has run — a rule that is silently different for CI and for a
# developer.
#
# So the repo keeps what it owns OUTSIDE this directory:
# `scripts/ratchets/cb200-baseline.json` is the CB-200 floor, next to the one
# script that reads it. `.pmat/project.toml` was left behind deliberately: it is
# pmat's own state file, pinned at version 3.7.1 against a 3.34.0 toolchain and
# carrying a `last_compliance_check` timestamp from April, so "hand-set config"
# describes one of its four lines.
**/.pmat/

# ── Derived pmat/pv caches (forjar#287, finished in forjar#401) ─────────────
# These are regenerated from the source tree on demand. Tracking them meant the
# working tree was NEVER clean: every commit rewrote them, every rebase
# conflicted on them, and `.pmat/baseline.json` alone churns ~3700 lines per
# commit.
#
# Measured cost during the 2026-08-25 defect sweep: five rebases blocked, two
# `git checkout` calls silently refused (their error swallowed by a `2>/dev/null`
# that made the failure look like success), and one branch left mid-rebase for
# several operations because of it.
#
# `.pmat/context.db-shm` and `-wal` are SQLite journal sidecars — tracking a live
# database's write-ahead log in git cannot be right under any policy.
#
# WHAT THE PREVIOUS VERSION OF THIS BLOCK CLAIMED, AND WHY IT WAS WRONG.
# It read "NOT ignored, deliberately: baseline.json, cb200-baseline.json,
# file-health-baseline.json, metrics/dependencies.json and project.toml" —
# and all five WERE matched by the rule above. gitignore does not un-track a
# file, so nothing visibly broke and the contradiction survived. Measured, it
# was not free: `.git/hooks/post-commit` regenerates `.pmat/baseline.json`
# after every commit and re-stages it, and `git add` on a tracked-and-ignored
# path prints "The following paths are ignored", exits 1, and STAGES IT ANYWAY
# — the exit code is cosmetic, which is precisely why the churn never stopped.
# Two `pmat tdg baseline create` runs over an unchanged tree differ in exactly
# one line, `created_at` (ZERO float drift, measured; no flag suppresses it),
# so every branch rewrites line 3 of a 1.2 MB file and any two-branch merge
# conflicts there. Two `.quorum` receipts in this tree name that conflict as
# the reason a re-anchor was needed, and the history carries 75 revisions of
# that one file.
#
# So every one of them is untracked. No in-repo consumer reads any of them: the
# pre-commit hook branches on `[ ! -f ... ]` and regenerates a missing baseline,
# and the one file that WAS load-bearing — the CB-200 ceiling — moved to
# `scripts/ratchets/cb200-baseline.json`, out of a directory pmat owns and
# ignores wholesale.
#
# tests/falsification_no_tracked_file_is_gitignored.rs pins the invariant: no
# path in the index may be matched by any ignore rule in effect, this file's or
# a nested one's.
.pmat/context.db
.pmat/context.db-shm
.pmat/context.db-wal
.pmat/context.idx/
.pmat/workspace.db
.pmat/workspace.idx/
.pmat/dead-code-cache.json
.pmat/deny-cache.txt
.pmat/deps-cache.json
.pmat/lint-cache.txt
.pmat/hooks-cache/
.pv/lint-previous.json

# pmat/hook scratch artifact, never part of the tree
test_repo/
